---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About DAC | Defence Aspirant Club">
  <main>
    <section class="border-t border-line px-5 py-18">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">---Who we are---</p>
        <h2>About DAC</h2>

        <p>
          Here we come together with like-minded people who are focused towards
          building themselves and growing together strong along with their buddies.
          We focus particularly on confidence building, communication skills and
          physical fitness. And help you prepare for a future in Defence along with
          guidance from your seniors where you learn from those who have walked the
          path before you.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-8">A Little About the History of Our Club</h3>

        <p>
          Our founder, <strong>Mr. Rajnish Kumar Singh</strong>, was recently
          commissioned into the Indian Navy as a <strong>Sub-Lieutenant</strong>,
          and many seniors are selected into the academies every year.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-2">To name a few:</p>

        <p>
          <strong>Cdt. Sawailal Suthar</strong> was recommended for the Indian Navy
          (SSC Tech) and the Air Force (NCC Special Entry).
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Cdt. Suyash Patil</strong> was recommended for the Indian Army
          (SSC Tech).
        </p>

        <div class="card-grid">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Our mission</h3>
            <p>
              Prepare aspirants for NDA, CDS, AFCAT, NCC Special Entry and SSB
              with honest guidance and regular practice.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>What we do</h3>
            <p>
              Fitness drills, mock GTO tasks, mock interviews, lectures by serving
              and retired personnel, and visits.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Who can join</h3>
            <p>
              Any student with a sincere interest in the forces. NCC cadets and
              non-cadets are both welcome.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>